\end{align}
is bounded away from zero (because $\alpha+\sigma\geq1$), a contradiction.

So, we get that $\liminf_{S\rightarrow \infty}\frac{(S\theta_c)^{\alpha}}{(S\theta_n)^{1-\sigma}}>0$. By combining this with 
(\ref{stheah}), we have that $S\theta_h$ is bounded from above and hence $\lim_{S\rightarrow \infty}\theta_h=0$.  Combining with (\ref{cn}), we obtain (\ref{ratio}).

