strong duality, in contrast with the Haar duality, where the Slater condition
does not ensure strong duality even in the case of semi-infinite linear
optimization. We apply extended concepts of uniform lower
semicontinuity of infinite
collections of functions, and establish general duality results via fuzzy multiplier
rules for infinite sums.
