\begin{remark}
\label{R6}
Assumption \ref{T5.1} in Theorem~\ref{optimality} can be
rewritten equivalently in the following way:
``\emph{the functions $f_{k}\,(k\in \mathbb{N}\cup\{0,\infty\})$ are lower semicontinuous and bounded from below on a \nbh\ of $\bx$, and the sets $\dom f_{k}$ are closed for all $k\in \mathbb{N}\cup\{\infty\}$ such that $\la_k=0$}''.

The closedness of the domains in the above condition is needed to ensure the lower semicontinuity of the functions $\lambda_{k}f_{k}\,(k\in \mathbb{N}\cup\{\infty\})$ when $\lambda_{k}=0$ for some $k\in \mathbb{N}\cup\{\infty\}$.
