    \cdot
    \frac{
    f_{X_0}(u_n(1+\theta_nt/r_n))
    }{
    f_{X_0}(u_n(1+t/r_n))
    }
    \\&
    \ \sim \
    t\cdot \xi(u_n(1+t/r_n))
    \\&
    \ \sim\
    t\cdot \xi(u_n)
    \,,
  \end{align*}
  where the last approximation uses that $\xi(x)\to \nu$ as $x\to\infty$.
  Thus, Assumption~\eqref{asu:derand:iii} is satisfied.
  Moreover, by the local uniformity of regularly varying functions,
  we have that for any sequence $(\tau_n)$ with $\tau_n\to 0$ as $n\to\infty$,
  \begin{align*}
    \frac{\PP[X_0>u_n]}{\PP[X_0>u_n(1\pm \tau_n)]}
