%\begin{srem}\label{name_weak_GR_sheaf}
%	This name ``weak GR-sheaf'' is in analogy with the characteristic zero picture (at least in the case of resolutions $\pi \colon X \to Y$). Indeed, in this case then $\pi_*\omega_X \inc \omega_Y$ is called the Grauert--Riemenschneider sheaf, because each map $H^i(Y, \pi_*\omega_Y) \to H^i(X, \omega_X)$ is an isomorphism du to Grauert--Riemenschneider vanishing (so in particular, $\chi(Y, \pi_*\omega_X) = \chi(X, \omega_X)$).
