\paragraph{Hiring committee.} The  algebra of coalitions  is the two-atom Boolean algebra $\mathbb{C}$ of the picture below. We let $\jty(\mathbb{C}) := \{\aga, \agb\}$. Since $W$ is the 8-element poset described in Section  \ref{interrogative:sec: hiring committee}, by Propositions \ref{interrogative:prop:charact meet-irr} and \ref{interrogative:prop:charact join-irr}, the lattice $E(W)$ has 127 completely meet-irreducible elements (coatoms) and 28 completely join-irreducible elements (atoms); 
