\begin{Exam}
	In this example, we illustrate how to associate a word $W_N(X)$ with a circular snake $X$ with nodal zones. Let $X$ be a circular snake with link as in Figure \ref{Fig. snake word circular}. We choose an orientation for $X$, fix a nodal zone $N$ and assign letters to the nodes by moving through the link of $X$, respecting this orientation, starting at $N$. In this case, using the alphabet $\{x_1, x_2,\ldots \}$, for the orientation $\varepsilon$ in Figure \ref{Fig. snake word circular}a, we obtain $$W_N(X) = [x_1x_2x_3x_4x_5x_6x_4x_2x_3x_5x_1x_6x_1].$$ 
    For the same orientation $\varepsilon$ but now starting from the node $N'$ in Figure \ref{Fig. snake word circular}a, we have $$W_{N'}(X) = [x_4x_2x_3x_5x_1x_6x_1x_2x_3x_4x_5x_6x_4].$$ 
    Finally, for the orientation $-\varepsilon$ and the node $N$ in Figure \ref{Fig. snake word circular}b, $$W_{N}(X) = [x_1x_2x_1x_3x_4x_5x_6x_2x_3x_6x_4x_5x_1].$$ 

