Consider $X$ the snake whose link is represented in both Figure \ref{5}a and Figure \ref{5}b. If $X=T(\gamma_1,\gamma_2)$ is oriented from $\gamma_1$ to $\gamma_2$, Figure \ref{5}a shows the corresponding arcs $\theta_i$ in nodal zones and hence the minimal sequence of $X$ is $\{0,3,6\}$. On the other hand, if $X=T(\gamma_2,\gamma_1)$ is oriented from $\gamma_2$ to $\gamma_1$, Figure \ref{5}b shows the corresponding arcs $\theta_i$ in nodal zones and hence the minimal sequence of $X$ is $\{0,2,5\}$.


