    Finally, let us prove that $\{X_i\}_{i=1}^{p+1}$ is minimal. By the construction of the minimal sequence of $X$, the Valette link of a single pancake cannot contain the pair $N_{j_{i-1}}, N_{j_{i}}$, $i=1,\ldots, p$, since it should be LNE. Hence, any pancake of $X$ must contain at most one $N_{j_{i}}$, and therefore any pancake decomposition of $X$ has at least $p+1$ pancakes.

