\hat{g} \ = \ &\frac{1}{2}\sum_{n=0}^3\sum_{f=0}^1\hat{Z}_{6n + 1 + 3f} \ , \nonumber \\
\hat{b} \ = \ &\frac{1}{2}\sum_{n=0}^3\sum_{f=0}^1 \hat{Z}_{6n + 2 + 3f} \ , \nonumber \\
\hat{Q}_{\text{tot}} \ = \  &\frac{1}{2}\sum_{n=0}^3\sum_{f=0}^1\sum_{c=0}^2 q_f \hat{Z}_{6n + 3f + c}  \ - \ \frac{1}{2}\sum_{n=0}^3 \hat{Z}_{25+2n}  \ ,
\end{align}
%
where $q_0 = 2/3$ is the electric charge of the up quark and $q_1 = -1/3$ is the electric charge of the down quark.
The initial state $|\Delta^- \Delta^-\rangle$ states used in our quantum simulations has $r=g=b=2$ and $Q_{\text{tot}}=-2$.
These charges are conserved under time evolution, but can be violated by device errors.
The results obtained from IonQ Forte Enterprise were post-selected to conserve these charges.


