Leakage and qubit loss errors in quantum computers lead to qubits becoming unresponsive to quantum gates. Undetected leakage errors can severely corrupt quantum computation, especially if they happen early in the circuit. In ion-trapped devices, leakage errors can happen due to the spontaneous emission and electronic transitions outside of the computational space.
Some known solutions use custom-designed gates that target the extended subspace to which the leakage occurs~\cite{Leakage2024}.
