\subsection{Additional Results on Interpretability}
Figures~\ref{app:inter_minist}, \ref{app:inter_cifar100}, and \ref{app:inter_imagenet} present additional visualization results of the error prediction tracing process on the MNIST, CIFAR-100, and Mini-ImageNet datasets, respectively. The first row displays examples of misclassified test samples, the second row shows the most influential training data for classifying these samples, and the third row presents the most harmful training data for these classifications. These visualization results allow us to trace the outcomes of the error prediction process effectively.

