The 1/3 rule demonstrated significant advantages over competing financial strategies:

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{50/30/20 Rule:} Allocating only 20\% of income to savings and debt repayment left households vulnerable to financial shocks, particularly those with high debt loads.
    \item \textbf{70/20/10 Rule:} This strategy, favoring higher spending on living expenses, often failed to create adequate buffers for emergencies or long-term planning.
