\subsubsection{Applications}
Theorem \ref{maintheorem1} is a  quite  flexible tool for  constructing $\RCD$ spaces as the following example illustrates.
\begin{example}Let $f: \mathbb S^1 \rightarrow (0, \infty)$ be smooth. For $K<0$ such that $-K$ is sufficiently large we have that $f'' \leq - Kf^2$.  If $K_F\geq K f^2$ for a constant $K_F\in \R$, then $K_F\geq \sup_B\{ (f')^2 + Kf^2\}$ (Proposition \ref{prop:albi2}). Then the $N$-warped product $B\times_f^\sN F$ satisfies the Riemannian curvature-dimension condition $\RCD(KN, N+1)$ for any compact $\RCD(K_F(N-1),N)$ space $F$.
\end{example}
