\begin{remark} If we assume that $B$ and $F$ are locally compact, complete, strictly intrinsic metric spaces, the existence of minimizing curves $\gamma=(\alpha, \beta)$ for $L$ is guaranteed by the Arzela-Ascoli theorem. In particular, one has the following corollary
