The viability of the LLMO in addressing constrained network optimization problems requires further investigation. The penalty method could be a promising approach for handling black-box constraints such as quality-of-experience requirements.
%Exploring the LLMO in conjunction with Lagrange duality analysis \cite{Boyd} would also be an interesting future work.

When LLMs are pretrained on a corpus specialized in the wireless communication field, we can leverage the prior knowledge developed by human engineers. This potentially enhances the optimization capabilities of the LLMO. Applying the LLMO framework to such telecom-specific foundation models \cite{TelecomGPT} would be an important future research direction.
