\begin{proof}[Proof of \autoref{lem:inf-dist-lb}]
Let $\vect{x} \in \ZZ\setminus \{\vect{0}\}$, and let $i \in [n]$ such that $\vect{x}_i\neq0$ and $(M\vect{x})_i \vect{x}_i \geq 0$ (\autoref{lem:P0nonneg}). Then $|( (M+qI_n)\vect{x})_i|= |(M\vect{x})_i + q\vect{x}_i| \geq q |\vect{x}_i| \geq q$. Invertibility of $M + qI_n$ follows from \autoref{lem:det-comp}.
\end{proof}


